.TH "FLOX\-SERVICES\-LOGS" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-services\-logs \- show logs of services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] services logs
     [\-d=<path> | \-r=<owner/name>]
     [\-\-follow]
     [\-n=<num>]
     [<name>] ...
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display the logs of the specified services.
.PP
If no services are specified, then the \f[CR]\-\-follow\f[R] flag is
required and logs from all services will be printed in real time.
.PP
One or more service names specified with the \f[CR]\-\-follow\f[R] flag
will follow the logs for the specified services.
.PP
If a service name is supplied without the \f[CR]\-\-follow\f[R] flag
then all of the available logs are displayed for that service.
If specified with the \f[CR]\-n\f[R] flag then only the most recent
\f[CR]<num>\f[R] lines from that service are displayed.
.PP
An error will be returned if a specified service does not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-follow\f[R]
Follow log output for the specified services.
Required when no service names are supplied.
.TP
\f[CR]\-n\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-tail\f[R]
Display only the last \f[CR]<num>\f[R] lines from the logs of the
specified services.
.TP
\f[CR]<name>\f[R]
Which service(s) to display logs for.
When omitted logs from all services will be displayed but the
\f[CR]\-\-follow\f[R] flag is required.
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
A FloxHub environment, specified in the form \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-default\f[R]
Use your default environment (\f[CR]<your\-user>/default\f[R]).
When unauthenticated in an interactive context, you will be prompted to
log in.
In non\-interactive contexts (e.g., scripts or CI), this flag will fail
with an error when authentication is missing.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
Follow logs for all services:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services logs \-\-follow
service1: hello
service2: hello
\&...
.EE
.PP
Follow logs for a subset of services:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services logs \-\-follow service1 service3
service1: hello
service3: hello
\&...
.EE
.PP
Display all available logs for a single service:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services logs myservice
starting...
running...
stopping...
completed
.EE
